[b]Hello, builder community friends![/b]

In the ongoing process of bringing you the best possible [b]DIORAMA BUILDER[/b] experience, we are releasing another PATCH with fixes and adjustments that we have detected are necessary, in addition to those that you requested on our Steam community.

For this help and your understanding, we would like to, once again, thank everyone who sent us feedback about the game and the DLCs.

Below is the list of improvements and fixes in this new PATCH:

[list]
[*] Fixed the issue that prevented version 1.0 from working on MAC OS. Now MAC users will be able to update to the new version and download and play the DLCs;
[*] Modified the Diorama Catalog and News storage system, which was previously on Google Drive and is now directly on Steam. This change allowed us to eliminate the LOADING screen for this information and fix problems that some players were having when LOADING DLCs and News, including for residents, mainly from China, who had access restrictions to Google Drive;
[*] Fixed the problem that caused the game to crash when trying to download several DLCs at the same time through the Dioramas Catalog;
[*] Fixed an issue that prevented, in some specific cases, that when finishing assembling a diorama, it would not switch to INTERACTIVE MODE;
[*] Solved the problem that prevented AUTOMATIC SAVE every 3 minutes during gameplay;
[*] Fixed the time counting system for assembling dioramas, which was calculating this time incorrectly;
[*] Made adjustments to the materials of some pieces that were too shiny and that made it difficult to see the mesh of pieces that were above them;
[*] Implemented several small adjustments to the game.
[/list]

Thank you very much for your continued support. This is what strengthens us and drives us to create increasingly better games for the community! Please keep sending us your valuable feedback!

Follow the studio's page to be notified about new DLCs and updates for Diorama Builder and new games from the studio.

Happy building!

